#N canvas 20 20 1600 1220 12;
#X text 20 20 m_nano -- the nanoKONTROL mapping layer. Decodes CC into named parameters on the disp bus and nothing else. It knows NOTHING about what it controls: that is the point of the m_ layer and the one boundary that is genuinely expensive to retrofit., f 58;
#X text 20 130 creation arg 1: the Pd channel that the nano's OWN channel 1 lands on. REQUIRED -- without it nothing decodes. The transport row is that channel plus one \, and this accepts BOTH. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 240 THE CHANNEL BLOCK IS PD'S INPUT SLOT \, not the device's position in the system MIDI list. Pd gives input slot n the channels (n-1)*16+1 upward \, so the nano is 17 on the Organelle (slot 2 \, per .pdsettings) and 1 on the Mac when it is the only input opened. MEASURED both ways rather than inferred -- and that is exactly why this is an argument and not a constant., f 58;
#X obj 20 400 ctlin;
#X obj 340 470 s \$0-cc;
#X obj 660 470 - \$1;
#X obj 660 520 t f f;
#X obj 660 570 >= 0;
#X obj 820 570 < 2;
#X obj 660 620 *;
#X obj 660 670 s \$0-nano-on;
#X text 660 720 TWO CHANNELS \, ONE FLAG. The offset is 0 for the control groups and 1 for the transport row \, so the gate is simply 0 <= offset < 2 -- and every other device in the rig falls outside it. The Launchpad sits 16 below and the 404 sits 16 above \, so neither can ever be mistaken for this one., f 44;
#N canvas 30 30 1300 900 controls 0;
#X text 20 20 Every control on the surface: nine sliders \, nine knobs \, eighteen buttons and the six transport keys. The value arrives LAST \, so the name and the two kind flags are already decoded and waiting by the time it gets here., f 58;
#X obj 20 140 inlet;
#X obj 20 190 spigot;
#X obj 160 150 r \$0-nano-on;
#X obj 20 250 t f f b;
#N canvas 30 30 2000 920 decode-name 0;
#X text 20 20 CC NUMBER IN \, A NAME AND TWO KIND FLAGS OUT -- all on \$0- sends \, because three results from one bang is what sends are for. Nothing in here touches the VALUE., f 58;
#X obj 20 150 inlet;
#X obj 20 200 f;
#X obj 160 160 r \$0-cc;
#X obj 20 250 t f f;
#X obj 20 310 div 10;
#X obj 20 360 t f f f;
#X obj 200 420 >= 2;
#X obj 200 460 s \$0-is-btn;
#X obj 380 420 < 2;
#X obj 380 460 s \$0-is-cont;
#X obj 560 310 mod 10;
#X obj 560 420 list prepend;
#X obj 560 480 route 0 1 2 3 4;
#X obj 560 550 makefilename slider-%d;
#X obj 560 600 s \$0-name;
#X obj 800 550 makefilename knob-%d;
#X obj 800 600 s \$0-name;
#X obj 1040 550 makefilename btn-t-%d;
#X obj 1040 600 s \$0-name;
#X obj 1280 550 makefilename btn-b-%d;
#X obj 1280 600 s \$0-name;
#X obj 1520 550 makefilename xport-%d;
#X obj 1520 600 s \$0-name;
#N canvas 40 40 900 620 unmapped 0;
#X text 20 20 A CC in this block that decodes to no known kind. It clears BOTH flags -- otherwise the arithmetic upstream would have left is-btn set \, and the next value would emit under the PREVIOUS control's name: plausible \, wrong \, and silent., f 52;
#X obj 20 120 inlet;
#X obj 20 170 t b b b;
#X msg 20 240 0;
#X obj 20 290 s \$0-is-cont;
#X msg 240 240 0;
#X obj 240 290 s \$0-is-btn;
#X obj 500 240 f;
#X obj 620 200 r \$0-cc;
#X obj 500 300 makefilename cc-%d-unmapped;
#X obj 500 350 list prepend warn m_nano;
#X obj 500 400 list trim;
#X obj 500 450 s err;
#X text 20 350 The clears come FIRST \, off the rightmost outlets \, and the error goes out last. Reversed \, a storm of unknown CCs could still leak one wrong parameter between the two., f 46;
#X text 20 500 THE list trim AGAIN. list prepend builds a list \; u_err's route matches a selector. Without it every m_nano warning would be dropped by the very bus that exists to stop things being silent., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 2 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 2 1 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 2 0 7 0;
#X connect 8 0 7 1;
#X connect 7 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X restore 1760 480 pd unmapped;
#X text 20 700 KIND AND WHICH \, PACKED \, THEN ROUTED. div 10 is the kind and mod 10 is which one -- the same idiom that already covers the Launchpad grid. Prepending the kind and routing on it gives each kind its OWN makefilename \, so there is no format to set and no ordering to get wrong., f 46;
#X text 620 700 THE TRANSPORT ROW IS JUST KIND 4. CC 41 to 46 give div 10 = 4 and mod 10 = 1 to 6 \, so it needs no separate path -- and because 4 is >= 2 it inherits the button treatment: press only \, no toggle \, no state. Folding it in deleted a whole subpatch., f 46;
#X text 1180 700 FIVE NAMES \, FIVE PLACEHOLDERS: slider-1 \, knob-3 \, btn-t-5 \, btn-b-9 \, xport-2. All named by PHYSICAL POSITION and never by function \, because what they do is decided in v0.3 -- and these five boxes are the seam where that arrives., f 46;
#X text 1180 860 route's REJECT outlet is the validity check: kinds 0 to 4 have a name \, anything else has not. No moses needed -- an earlier attempt added one and shifted every box index underneath it., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 1 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 2 12 1;
#X connect 6 1 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 6 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 4 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 15 0;
#X connect 13 1 16 0;
#X connect 16 0 17 0;
#X connect 13 2 18 0;
#X connect 18 0 19 0;
#X connect 13 3 20 0;
#X connect 20 0 21 0;
#X connect 13 4 22 0;
#X connect 22 0 23 0;
#X connect 13 5 24 0;
#X restore 700 310 pd decode-name;
#X obj 100 340 r \$0-is-cont;
#X obj 20 400 spigot;
#X obj 440 340 r \$0-is-btn;
#X obj 360 400 spigot;
#X obj 360 450 select 127;
#X msg 360 500 1;
#X obj 20 570 list prepend;
#X obj 560 530 r \$0-name;
#X obj 20 620 list trim;
#X obj 20 730 s disp;
#X text 820 400 The decode runs off the RIGHTMOST outlet \, so it has finished before either gate sees the value. That is why this needs no delay object anywhere., f 46;
#X text 20 810 ONE EMIT CHAIN \, FED BY TWO GATES. A fan-IN needs no trigger -- only a fan-out does -- so the continuous value and the button's 1 converge on the same list prepend \, whose cold inlet already holds the name., f 46;
#X text 420 810 EVERY BUTTON EMITS ON PRESS ONLY \, the transport row included. They are momentary \, 127 then 0 \, measured on this unit. Pd owns any state because the mk1 has no host-controllable LEDs \, so device-side state would silently desync., f 46;
#X text 820 810 THE list trim IS LOAD-BEARING. list prepend makes a LIST \, and g_oled's route matches a SELECTOR \, so without it every parameter is silently rejected and the display just shows zero., f 46;
#X obj 20 670 t a a;
#X obj 300 730 s param;
#X text 560 620 TWO BUSES OFF ONE TRIGGER \, added in Phase 5. param is the control CHANGING \; disp is a request to SHOW it. The action goes out of the right outlet first and the report second -- the same order u_init uses for its stages. Duplicating the data here beats teaching a hardware-verified display file a second bus., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 2 5 0;
#X connect 4 1 9 0;
#X connect 4 0 7 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 1;
#X connect 8 0 9 1;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 7 0 12 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 13 0 12 1;
#X connect 12 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 20 0;
#X connect 20 0 15 0;
#X connect 20 1 21 0;
#X restore 20 540 pd controls;
#X obj 1180 400 loadbang;
#X obj 1180 440 del 2000;
#X obj 1180 480 f \$1;
#X obj 1180 520 print m_nano-control-channel;
#X text 1180 570 Says which block it is listening on \, once \, a couple of seconds in. THE DELAY IS NOT COSMETIC: deploy.sh gates on OUTPUT rather than exit status \, and quits the check immediately after load \, so a print at loadbang would fail every deploy. This way the diagnostic survives where it is needed -- the by-hand SSH console -- and the check stays silent., f 40;
#X text 20 800 WHAT IS NOT HERE: any notion of what a control DOES. Names are generated from physical position -- slider-1 \, knob-3 \, xport-2 -- and that is deliberate \, because there are no parameters to name until v0.3. A lookup table pretending to be a mapping would be a lie \; generated names are honest about being placeholders., f 58;
#X text 20 940 NOTHING HERE DRIVES mode \, start OR stop \, and that is deliberate. The transport row was briefly a mode toggle \; it is being repurposed as scene selection \, so it now gets ordinary CC treatment like every other button. What ends up driving those buses is a Phase 5 or 6 decision -- tracked in plan-v04.md., f 58;
#X text 860 900 ctlin's outlets are value \, controller \, channel \, and Pd fires RIGHT TO LEFT -- so channel lands \, then the controller \, then the value that triggers everything. VERIFIED off the wire rather than assumed: the very first event of a session already carries the right controller and channel \, which cannot happen unless both were stored first. This repo has been bitten here before \, by polytouchin emitting note before value., f 46;
#X connect 3 0 12 0;
#X connect 3 1 4 0;
#X connect 3 2 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 1 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 9 1;
#X connect 6 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 15 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
